# <unit> <run|crash|timeout> <max_failures>  (wine-pe/tests/kernel32.sh --baseline)
# Measured on the linux-cross CI job (WINETEST kernel32:<unit> lines). 0-failure run units are the allowlist;
# a unit may only move up: fewer failures, or crash/timeout -> run. Never raise a number to make a run pass.
# crash and timeout gate the same (the unit must not complete); a unit near the 30 s cap flips between them.
# file: 191 and 222 failures were both observed on identical code, so the larger one is the budget.
actctx crash 0
atom run 0
change run 0
codepage run 0
comm run 0
console run 1
debugger timeout 0
directory run 0
drive run 2
environ run 10
fiber run 7
file run 162
format_msg run 0
generated run 0
heap crash 0
loader crash 0
locale run 297
mailslot run 15
module crash 0
path run 0
pipe crash 0
power run 0
process crash 0
profile run 4
resource run 7
sync crash 0
thread crash 0
time run 34
timer crash 0
toolhelp crash 0
version run 8
virtual crash 0
# volume: 35 -> 39 by the object manager namespace (docs/slices/om.md): volume.c:165 and :200 are todo_wine because Wine fails
# them and Windows passes; \??\Y: made by DefineDosDevice is a real symbolic link now, so they pass and Wine's harness counts
# "succeeded inside todo" as failures. The guest sees its own drives (C:) in \??, not the Wine prefix's, so the Z: cases are gone.
volume run 39
